      "message": "\u003eI thought the approach we agreed upon in last week\u0027s meeting was that we would be deleting files at the beginning of a build, instead of at the end of one?\n\nYes we agreed on deleting at the beginning, sorry I thought that would be another CL to delete all the metrics and I did not relate it to this CL. Updated to delete it at the beginning.\n\n\n\u003eWouldn\u0027t deleting this file here result in the file never being uploaded via the uploader? Because the file will no longer be around when we call UploadMetrics.\n\nDo you mind letting me know why the file will no longer be around when we call UploadMetrics? From my understanding, with the \u0027defer\u0027 function, it will be the last one to execute. Do I miss anything here?\n\n\u003eIt\u0027s also a problem to delete this file after we call uploadMetrics, because:\nUploadMetrics runs in the background and may not have finished by the time we delete the metrics file\nCI bots don\u0027t do metrics uploading in the same way -- they upload the entire contents of their logs directory at the end of the build\nThe end user may want to manually inspect metrics files, which will no longer be around if we delete them here.\n\nThe above three points are solid reasons and we should put it at the beginning. Thanks for pointing out.",
